THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

Some parts of this repository belong to others and keep their own terms.
Nothing above changes those terms.

- Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, under the Open Database
  License (ODbL) 1.0: roads, water, places, land use and glaciers. Data
  files in public/data that are built from OpenStreetMap or Microsoft
  data are made available under the ODbL 1.0.
- Elevation behind the terrain in public/data/state from AWS Terrain
  Tiles (Tilezen Joerd, on the Registry of Open Data on AWS): 3DEP
  (formerly NED), GMTED2010 and SRTM terrain data courtesy of the U.S.
  Geological Survey, in the public domain.
- Building outlines from Microsoft US Building Footprints, under the
  ODbL 1.0.
- Storm drain, road and stream data from the City of Bonney Lake and
  Pierce County GIS, used under each provider's terms and provided as
  is, without warranty.
- Storm drain data from the City of Federal Way GIS, provided as is,
  without warranty of any kind. The City of Federal Way prohibits
  commercial use or sale of its data without written authorization.
- Storm drain data from the City of Sammamish GIS, used under the city's
  terms: provided as is, without warranty or any representation of
  accuracy, timeliness or completeness.
- Storm drain data from the City of Mercer Island, City of Maple Valley
  and City of Covington GIS, used under each provider's terms and
  provided as is, without warranty. The City of Mercer Island makes no
  representation or warranty about the accuracy or currency of its GIS
  data.
- Storm drain data from the City of Shoreline, City of Lake Forest Park
  and City of Kenmore GIS, used under each provider's terms and provided
  as is, without warranty of any kind. The City of Shoreline notes that
  its data is not official.
- Salmon and steelhead distribution data (coho statewide, in Pierce
  County and in public/data/salmon) from SWIFD, the Statewide Washington
  Integrated Fish Distribution of the Washington Department of Fish and
  Wildlife and the Northwest Indian Fisheries Commission, used under
  WDFW's terms and provided as is, without warranty.
- Stream and lake data from the USGS National Hydrography Dataset, place
  outlines from the US Census Bureau, and Natural Earth data, all in the
  public domain.
- The Silkscreen font by Jason Kottke and the Geist font by Vercel, under
  the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
- npm packages, including Firebase, under their own licenses.


